  "body": "Found while working #982. Part of #882 (its knife edge 3, \"Rotary travel pins\", which was not filed).\n\n**What happens.** With the microlift acceptance settled (#982), the rotary Adaptive pins still turn on nanometres through the #850 planning budget. On unchanged upstream/main 3e9b8ae1 (release, Linux x86-64), with only `rings::open` eroding N nm deeper than it dilates back:\n\n| fixture | level | 0 nm | 16 nm | 250 nm |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| r7 bar (`adaptive_plans_the_developed_levels_under_the_load_and_kink_laws`) | 5.0 | refused past the budget (85-86 revolutions), rings | refused, rings | **the budget passes it: HSM-planned, 5 in-cut breaks of 5.0-6.2 deg - the pin is red** (on main and with #982's fix alike) |\n| r7 bar | 5.5 | HSM, lifted | HSM, lifted | main: rings (refused for travel - the lift edge #982 fixes); with #982: HSM, lifted |\n| window (`the_developed_window_reaches_the_planner_and_names_each_refusal`) | 6.0, 5.0 | refused past the budget after 86 revolutions | refused after 85 | **the budget passes them**: main refuses them for travel (the lift edge); with #982 they are HSM-planned at 18.8 % D, 0 breaks |\n\nSo `adaptive_plans_the_developed_levels_under_the_load_and_kink_laws` is green on main only because the budget refuses level 5.0 at this exact geometry; a 250 nm change of the rings lets it through, it is planned, and the pin fails on the kink law (the breaks themselves are #1050).\n\n**Why it matters.** Same as #982: a plan choice that flips on a nanometre-scale input blocks #882 and any other change to the planner's geometry, and a pin that is green by coincidence proves nothing.\n\n**What #982 does and does not do.** It removes the lift-acceptance edge (the r6.2 neck levels 5.7 / 5.2 are HSM-planned at every perturbation tried). It does not touch `budget.rs` or `grow.rs` (PR #953 owns the latter).\n\nDone means: the budget's verdict on the rotary window's and the r7 bar's levels is the same under a 16 nm - 0.25 um perturbation of the openings, pinned by perturbed twins the way #982 pins the slot; whichever way level 5.0 of the r7 bar is decided, its pin states it.\n",
